    <title>Past Medical History</title>
    <text><paragraph>Historical biography with true dates. These events are not part of the synthetic care timeline.</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Historical date</th><th>History</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1833 or 1834</td><td>Collapse with violent headache, dizziness, and trembling while working in the August heat, followed by kicks and a blow to the head</td><td>D (CLM-0006)</td></tr><tr><td>1836</td><td>Kick to the left eye in an assault at a Baltimore shipyard; the eye was closed and badly swollen</td><td>D (CLM-0008)</td></tr><tr><td>September 16, 1843</td><td>Broken right hand in a mob assault; the bones were not properly set, and the hand did not recover its natural strength and dexterity</td><td>D (CLM-0011)</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

