<component><section><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.17" extension="2015-08-01"/><code code="29762-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Social history Narrative"/><title>Social History</title><text><list><item>Editor and publisher of a weekly newspaper he founded, author of a published memoir, and a public speaker who travels most months to give talks; writes by hand for several hours most days and often late into the night [S]</item><item>Sources of strength and support he names: his work and his writing, which he describes as his purpose; his marriage and their five children at home; the people he works with in his community; and his faith and his church [S]</item><item>Has faced racial discrimination and threats of violence in public life, including at speaking events; is watchful when traveling and plans his routes and companions with care [S]</item><item>Does not drink alcohol (AUDIT-C 0); never used tobacco or other drugs; no firearms at home [S]</item><item>Taught himself to read and write as a boy and regards literacy as the way he made his own life [S]</item></list></text></section></component>

